{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.PathConnected","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.IsolatedZeros"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.eqOn_of_analyticOnNhd_of_eventuallyEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.eqOn_of_analyticOnNhd_of_eventuallyEq","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L145-L152","doc":"The same statement phrased against `cLiTwoExt` itself: two analytic functions\non `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` agreeing near `0` agree everywhere on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.eqOn_cLiTwoExt_hypotheses_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.eqOn_cLiTwoExt_hypotheses_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** `eqOn_cLiTwoExt_of_eqOn_ball` is universally quantified over\n`g`, and a uniqueness theorem whose hypotheses nothing satisfies proves nothing.\nThey are satisfiable: `cLiTwoExt` itself meets them.\n\nThe check with real bite is numerical and lives in Route 23 G1: mpmath's\n`polylog(2, ·)` is an **independently implemented** analytic continuation\n(functional equations and series acceleration, nothing to do with this integral),\nso uniqueness predicts it must agree with `cLiTwoExt` everywhere off the cut. It\ndoes — to 30 dps at `‖y‖ = 40`, far outside the disc where the series diverges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.eqOn_cLiTwoExt_of_eqOn_ball","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.eqOn_cLiTwoExt_of_eqOn_ball","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L113-L130","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt` is the unique analytic extension of the series.**\n\nIf `g` is analytic on `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` and agrees with `cLiTwo` on the open unit disc,\nthen `g = cLiTwoExt` on all of `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`.\n\nThe identity theorem, with `z₀ = 0`: agreement on a whole disc is far more than\nthe accumulation it needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isPreconnected_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isPreconnected_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L107-L109","doc":"**`ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` is preconnected** — the hypothesis the identity theorem wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isPathConnected_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isPathConnected_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L103-L105","doc":"**`ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` is path-connected.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.starConvex_zero_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.starConvex_zero_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L81-L101","doc":"**`ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` is star-convex about `0`** — the piece Mathlib does not have.\n\nIf `b·w` were on the cut for some `b ∈ (0,1]`, it would be real and `≥ 1`, hence\n`w` real with `w = (b·w)/b ≥ 1/b ≥ 1`: `w` was on the cut to begin with. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.zero_mem_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.zero_mem_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L78-L79","doc":"**`0 ∈ ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.notCut_eq_preimage_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.notCut_eq_preimage_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmUnique.lean#L60-L76","doc":"`ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` is the image of Mathlib's slit plane under `w ↦ 1 − w`.\n\nRecorded because it explains why the star centre here is `0` where Mathlib's is\n`1`: the two sets are exchanged by that involution, which sends `1 ↦ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}